.git
.gitignore
.workbuddy
.workbuddy-ai
.arts
.codeartsdoer
.freebuff
# Local scratch: a PostgreSQL data directory, live SQLite databases holding the
# admin and test accounts, the bearer token, both test-account passwords, and
# run logs. `.gitignore` covers `.gates/` but this file is a separate list, and
# `COPY . /app` is the only copy instruction — so without the line below a build
# bakes all of it into the image, which contradicts the Dockerfile's own
# statement that "Admin credentials are NOT baked into the image".
# `tests/unit/test_ignore_files.py` keeps the two lists in step.
.gates
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.log
output_img
user_upload_images
admin_data
# Runtime task storage: user-uploaded photos and results — must not enter the image
storage
output
weights
# Model weights are distributed separately (see .gitignore) and must never be
# baked into an image. These patterns need the `**/` prefix: a bare `*.pt`
# anchors to the context root in Docker's ignore syntax, so it excluded nothing
# under Global/checkpoints/ or Face_Enhancement/checkpoints/ and both trees were
# copied into the worker image (measured: 2.1 GB + 704 MB of .pt/.pth inside
# fiximg-worker:ci). The root-anchored forms are kept for files that really do
# sit at the top level.
**/*.pth
**/*.pt
**/*.dat
**/*.ckpt
**/*.onnx
*.pth
*.pt
*.dat
*.ckpt
*.onnx
test_images/gpu_smoke_in
test_images/gpu_smoke_out
test_images/gpu_smoke_out2
test_images/detect_smoke_out

# Tracked in git, deliberately not in the image. The Dockerfile's only copy
# instruction is `COPY . /app`, so everything not listed above is baked in.
#
# tests/  1.0 MB, 1517 tests. CI runs them (`.github/workflows/ci.yml` lints and
#         runs pytest over this path), and the Dockerfile neither installs the
#         `test` extra nor runs pytest, so nothing at build or run time needs
#         them. `tests/unit/test_ignore_files.py` asserts the CI still points
#         here, so "not in the image" cannot quietly become "not in the project".
# docs/   12.9 MB, of which 12.7 MB is images. The prose is the API contract
#         (docs/api.md), the deployment guide and the project audit log; the
#         images are the README gallery and upstream comparison shots. The
#         Gradio Examples tab does NOT read these -- it serves the root
#         `examples/` directory, which stays in the image.
#
# Deliberately NOT added to .gitignore: both are tracked source. Excluding them
# from git would delete the project's only evidence that any of this works.
tests
docs
# Working directories, not source. `_audit/` holds the local scan ledgers and
# scratch probes, `reports/` the generated audit reports; both are produced
# beside the project and change on every session, so baking them into a
# published image ships review notes nobody outside this checkout can act on.
# They are listed here rather than in .gitignore because they are evidence of
# work done, not build inputs.
_audit
reports


# ---------- Local pollution (P5) ----------
# The root Dockerfile builds with `COPY . /app`, so anything left in the context
# ends up in the published image. These names appear at the repository root when
# a path built from an unset variable (`%SystemDrive%`, `~`) or an interrupted pip
# build is used as a directory name; they were moved out of the tree in the P5
# remediation and these patterns keep a future run from baking them back in.
#
# Docker's ignore syntax anchors a pattern to the context root only with a
# leading slash or an explicit `**/`. These are written root-anchored so a
# legitimate directory that happens to share the name deeper in the tree is not
# silently dropped from the build context.
/%SystemDrive%
/undefined
/~
/pip-build-env-*
/pip-build-tracker-*
/pip-ephem-wheel-cache-*
/pip-install-*

# A quarantine accidentally created inside the tree must never be shipped.
/publication_quarantine_*
